From ff9603c17efd28a28531e4fe4d2ebedb45e838e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Wohl <wohl@awohl.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:07:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Cogit: store the followed literal with the store check

Cogit>>indexForSelector:in:at: scans the literal frame of a sending
method.  A literal that is a forwarder (left by become:) is followed,
and the followed object is written back into the method with
objectMemory longAt:put:.  This store skips the store check.

The sending method is usually old.  When become: made an old literal
into a forwarder to a young object, the old method now refers to a
young object but is not in the remembered set.  The next scavenge
neither updates nor traces the literal.  The young object moves or
dies, and the literal keeps a stale address.  A later full GC can then
stop with a segmentation fault in markAndTrace or in
fixFollowedField:ofObject:withInitialValue:.

The method is reached from relocateIfCallOrMethodReference:mcpc:delta:
during compactCogCompiledCode.

Write the followed literal with storePointer:ofObject:withValue:.  This
remembers the method when the method is old and the value is young.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 smalltalksrc/VMMaker/Cogit.class.st | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smalltalksrc/VMMaker/Cogit.class.st b/smalltalksrc/VMMaker/Cogit.class.st
index f6e70810e..5722ccba0 100644
--- a/smalltalksrc/VMMaker/Cogit.class.st
+++ b/smalltalksrc/VMMaker/Cogit.class.st
@@ -8092,8 +8092,11 @@ Cogit >> indexForSelector: selector in: cogMethod at: mcpc [
 				                 + objectMemory baseHeaderSize + methodOop.
 			(objectMemory isOopForwarded: methodLiteral) ifTrue: [ 
 				methodLiteral := objectMemory followForwarded: methodLiteral.
-				objectMemory longAt: (i * objectMemory bytesPerOop
-				                 + objectMemory baseHeaderSize + methodOop) put: methodLiteral].
+				"The method is usually old and the followed literal can be young (a become
+				 of an old object into a young one).  Only storePointer:ofObject:withValue:
+				 adds the method to the remembered set; a plain longAt:put: leaves the method
+				 pointing at a young object that the next scavenge moves."
+				objectMemory storePointer: i ofObject: methodOop withValue: methodLiteral].
 
 			methodLiteral = selector ifTrue: [ 
 				self assert:
-- 
